            "cites": [4]
          },
          {
            "text": "In June 2026, it was reported that about one-third of units in the city's master leasing program, around 250, remained vacant under her tenure.",
            "cites": [2]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "On housing, in 2025 Bass supported the city council in opposing a state bill that would allow dense housing near transit stations, urging the governor to veto it. The governor signed the bill into law in October 2025. In April 2026, she signed an executive order to speed up residential construction by studying reforms such as self-certification.",
        "cites": [2],
